&gt; I can see no reason why god would punish this child so. Her mother is a fully believing devout Christian, trying her best. Same with her father. I’ve explained my agnosticism with them, but bless their souls, they insist that god has a plan for all of us, and something good will come from all of this child’s suffering 

&amp;#x200B;

God bless your uncle and aunt for their continuing faith in Him.

&amp;#x200B;

&gt;  If I was god, I would end this child’s suffering, as she is too young to understand why it is happening, and is living a hell every day. There’s a very high chance that she won’t even make it anyway. So I find it kind of mean to let a child suffer just to teach *us* some lesson should we survive her.  

&amp;#x200B;

You are not God. You cannot make a star. You cannot set the boundaries of the oceans. You cannot even name 1/10th of the animals that exist. Yet you insist here that God is trying to teach us some lesson through the child's suffering as though He has gotten it wrong.

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; I have a hard time forgiving god for this child’s suffering and I’m terrified of hell 

&amp;#x200B;

I understand. But it is not God who makes the child suffer. It is the sickness in the child that causes the suffering. It is God whom feels compassion for the child. It is God whom says 'I will have faith that the Lord will deliver my child from their afflictions.'

It is God who hopes for a better outcome for the child. It is God who loves the child. You love the child. We love the child. God is love.

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; i want to avoid hell at all costs. 

&amp;#x200B;

Visit the child in their sickness. Gladden their hearts. Make them smile. In this way you will avoid hell and be the hands and feet God needs to deliver His message of love to the child.

&amp;#x200B;

Ok

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; The Bible is the foundation for believing the Christian god exists. 

mm, actually it is Jesus' testimony which validates the existence of the Christian God. Sure this is written and forms part of the canon but it would have been (and indeed was and is) just as powerful (if not more powerful) as the spoken word articulated by an existing believer. This is why the Apostles were the founders of the Church of Christ.

I'm being a bit nitpicky sure but I think this is important to understand. The bible is validated by the Spirit of God whom the believer receives. The bible does not in and of itself validate God. It is faith that validates God and faith that testifies to the truth of the bible.

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; God is absent and does not work miracles today. 

&amp;#x200B;

Not true. Seen with my own eyes. Not stuff that could be easily interpreted as an act of nature either. Like the wound from a nail through the foot of a skeptic just disappearing when they came to a worship meeting with me for example. I mean it just disappeared. As did his limp and pain.

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; Christians do not work greater miracles than Jesus, or *any* miracles at all. 

Again this is false. I have seen some amazing things Christians have done in the name of Christ. Too many to mention. You may accuse me of lying to support my position but really for what purpose? I don't want to support a false hope. That is the last thing I want believe me.

&amp;#x200B;

God is very much alive in His believers. His Spirit is doing many great things through the body of Christ who are the believers. God is love. Where you see love, you see God.

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; How do you know there's a soul to nourish? 

I wish I had followed my instincts and typed this above in r/test before you had a chance to reply because I knew it was coming :)

&amp;#x200B;

When I look in the mirror, I can see my soul through my eyes. If they are happy eyes then my soul is full of light. If they are angry hateful eyes then I have replaced the light with darkness and my soul is sad.

Maybe you dont think you have a soul or dont care or whatever, but this is my experience. I only speak about what I know and can testify to without there being a valid accusation of 'false' against it.

&amp;#x200B;

&gt; would it be more correct to say you think about it and see how it makes you feel? 

&amp;#x200B;

If you like.

&amp;#x200B;

What would be a good Christian slogan that I could put on a bumper sticker?
Hi,

&amp;#x200B;

I am asking for a decent original Christian bumper sticker slogan for my car.

&amp;#x200B;

If any are submitted and voted upon then I will take the one with the highest votes in 7 days time and gild the entry with gold.

&amp;#x200B;

The Rules

\---------------

1. Must be original
2. Must relate to the Christian faith in a positive way.
3. It can contain direct scripture but not just be scripture. So this would be allowed ... "Love is Patient and Kind. Have you been patient and kind today?" but "Love is patient, love is kind. It does not envy, it does not boast, it is not proud." would be considered unoriginal content since the whole thing is quoted directly from scripture and would fall outside the rules as stated.
4. Must be no longer than 21 words as printing may get a little difficult.

&amp;#x200B;

As always, if this is deemed inappropriate by the moderators, please accept my apologies and remove at will

&amp;#x200B;

EDIT: Apologies for cutting the time short but I must for various personal reasons. Congratulations to our tireless moderator u/righteous_dude for his great entry. 

&amp;#x200B;

Thanks all for having me :)

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

Following Christ , carrying your cross, suffering trials and tribulations, putting your faith above everything else etc. is hard. I am not surprised some seeds fell on rocky ground so to speak. But it is OK. People who say 'Enough of this!' have my compassion. Hopefully the things they do in their secular lives are still fruitful and they do not actually turn to the dark side (sorry been helping my youngest son play Star Wars - The Force Unleashed :-) )

&amp;#x200B;

Sometimes people struggle in their secular lives and then seek out their faith again to help them overcome their struggles. God doesn't mind. He welcomes everyone.

Congratulations on having the most voted entry. 

&amp;#x200B;

I am afraid I had to cut the time short as I have some pressing matters to attend to and will not have time for Reddit for the foreseeable future.

&amp;#x200B;

Peace to all and thank you for having me :)

&amp;#x200B;

May the Lord bless you all and make His face to smile upon you..
